[00:04] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: A man wearing FPV goggles and holding a controller, with a woman beside him.
AUDIO: '[music] Welcome to the Anti-Gravity A1 flight mode tutorial. The Anti-gravity A1 features two distinct flight modes. Let\'s take a look'

[00:16] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Split screen showing a hand holding the controller and the FPV goggles interface with drone view.
AUDIO: 'at both. [music] In this mode, the navigation point in the goggles interface follows your hand gestures and the drone\'s orientation synchronizes with that point.'

[00:29] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Split screen showing controller movement and corresponding drone movement in FPV view.
AUDIO: 'Move your arm left and the navigation point will then move left, meaning the drone will turn [music] left. Raise your arm upward and the point moves upward. Pull the accelerator trigger, [music]'

[00:44] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Split screen showing controller movement and corresponding drone movement in FPV view.
AUDIO: 'the drone will fly toward the navigation point upwards. The same principle applies to right and downward movements. During flight, [music] you can freely look around to'

[00:56] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Man wearing FPV goggles, with the FPV view showing the drone's perspective. Man wearing FPV goggles, with the FPV view showing the drone's perspective.
AUDIO: 'see a full 360° view. As long as the navigation points position doesn\'t change, the drone\'s flight direction remains steady. [music]'

[01:08] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Man wearing FPV goggles, with the FPV view showing "navigation assist" and the drone's forward view.
AUDIO: 'When your viewing angle differs from the flight direction, navigation assist will appear at the top of the screen, showing the view directly ahead of the drone to help you monitor your flight path. [music]'

[01:21] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: Close-up of the controller, highlighting buttons and dials.
AUDIO: 'If the flight direction does not align with where you are looking, you can press the 360 view dial to quickly rotate the drone\'s nose to match your current view. This mode is ideal for stable everyday'

[01:35] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: FPV goggles menu interface, showing options like "Return to Home," "Deep Track," "Sky Game," "Sky Path," and "FPV Mode."
AUDIO: 'shooting and suits most flight scenarios. [music] Select FPV mode from the top [music] right corner of the vision goggles menu.'

[01:49] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: Man and woman observing the Antigravity A1 drone flying.
AUDIO: 'In FPV mode, the steering controls change. [music] Rotate your wrist left to turn the grip controller left [music] and the drone'

[02:02] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Split screen showing wrist rotation of the controller and the drone turning. Split screen showing wrist rotation of the controller and the drone turning.
AUDIO: 'will turn left. Rotate your wrist right and the drone will turn right. [music] Note that swinging your arm horizontally'

[02:17] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Man and woman, with FPV view showing the drone flying over a landscape.
AUDIO: 'will not turn the drone in this mode. Unless you turn your head, the flight view will always display the forward direction. All other operations remain consistent'

[02:30] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: Man and woman looking up at the drone flying near a wind turbine. Split screen showing controller and FPV view with on-screen elements.
